Good. I found the schema rule for the github tracker binding. Lines 1433-1458 show:

```json
{
  "if": {
    "properties": {
      "tracker_binding": {
        "const": "github"
      }
    }
  },
  "then": {
    "properties": {
      "beads_linkage": {
        "const": null
      },
      "github_publication": {
        "properties": {
          "mode": {
            "enum": [
              "issue",
              "issue_and_projects"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

So when `tracker_binding` is set to `"github"`, the `github_publication.mode` field is constrained to either `"issue"` or `"issue_and_projects"`. This means an unpublished node with `github_publication.mode: "local_only"` would violate the schema if I tried to set `tracker_binding: "github"` on it.

Now I need to prepare the goal_seek files by creating the first line of intermediate.jsonl before running the Skill, then execute the two Skills.

I'll set up the goal_seek files in the FIXTURE_BEADS's eval-log directory, making sure the directory exists first.

